A||||25||Smokey||Mistaken for an import?||||1||
Z||000000||Smokey||01-02-2000||04:35 AM||||has anyone else ran into this problem. I've had many people mistake my car for an import. It seems like if someone lays eyes on a two seater it's automatically an import or something. I know fiero's aren't common or anything, but come on! Then i had someone ask me why i was copying off of MR2 with 2M4 on my car! think im gonna go get a sticker for my back window that says "LiL american import" :-)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||08:33 AM||||Just gently remind them that the Fiero 2m4 was around before the MR2 was even in diapers!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||01-02-2000||11:26 AM||||When I bought my first Fiero, I had to borrow a little money from my grandfather to make it happen.  He was a West Virginia coal miner and never bought anything that wasn't made in the USA if he could help it (no one had to tell him to remember Pearl Harbor - he never forgot it!).  He thought the Fiero was a rebadged import (like the Pontiac LeMans), and wouldn't lend me the cash until I showed him a magazine article proving the Fiero was made in Michigan.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||01-02-2000||07:20 PM||||I find that most people remember the fiero but only the older notchbacks. When Iam in my 86SE thats when they ask what is it and what year?, I think its the aero fascia that throws them off. I have had the toyota thing said about my car too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||01-02-2000||09:51 PM||||Dont think import. Think Exotic.  Alot of exotics have been made over seas but we have a fair share of them. Some of the better ones I think but that is just me.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||01-04-2000||03:25 AM||||A few months ago, while driving my '88 Formula, an older lady commented on the "nice little Triumph" I was driving.   ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||01-04-2000||05:09 AM||||Tom's right.  I love my Fieros, but a nice Lotus Esprit V8 or McLaren F1 would look good in my driveway, too.  (Behind the Fiero, of course! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
