Z||000014||DRH||01-05-2000||02:47 PM||||Check out the site below. According to it there is no such material as enduraflex, only a marketing term. I believe the hood, roof, upper rear piece (Fastback vs. Notchback) and the trunk are made of what is commonly refered to as fiberglass.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/enduraflex.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/enduraflex.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||mutfish||01-05-2000||03:05 PM||||The info in the above site is correct according to the 88 service manual...but the manual also points to the headlite doors and lists them as being made of sheet molded compound.I just painted my GT this past summer,and know for a fact they are metal...aluminum,I think...<p>[This message has been edited by mutfish (edited 01-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||mrfiero||01-05-2000||09:15 PM||||Sheet molded compound (SMC) is not the same as fiberglass!  There is absolutely no fiberglass in any Fiero.  The roof, decklid and hood are made from SMC, which is very similar looking to fiberglass.  <P>The entire body of the Fiero is made from plastic (SMC, RIM, RRIM, etc.....SMC is derived from plastic not glass fiber.<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DJRice||01-06-2000||09:57 AM||||I have a cracked headlight door off an 85 that isnt metal, so maybe the changed them when they changed the motor assemblies or something.||||reg||1
Z||000018||mutfish||01-06-2000||10:57 AM||||Just to satisfy my curiousity,does anyone know what years/material,the headlamp doors were made from? Like I said, my '88s are metal...||||reg||1
Z||000019||ChadMan||01-06-2000||01:52 PM||||My 84's headlamp doors were made of pot metal, with painted fiberglass caps that appeared to be glued on.  (I'll let you know what the 88's are made of if/when I ever have problems with them.)||||reg||1
Z||000020||DRH||01-06-2000||02:42 PM||||OK, maybe I should have said the SMC stuff LOOKS like fiberglass when it is broken.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000021||DJRice||01-07-2000||01:09 PM||||That would explain it if they have figerglass caps, because it was the end of one of mine that was broken.  I never really paid much attention to them other then the one with the busted end||||reg||1
Z||000022||william_thorniii||01-07-2000||01:29 PM||||When I go to a particular pizza establishment in Cincinnati, I always get two pizzas (the second is always half price) since usually my fiancee and I can only finish 1 (and she doesn't help much only eating 2 pieces of a large) so we take the other one home.  In the parking lot, I was putting the pizza on top of the spare tire and some kids were nearby.  I heard one exclaim "Wow!  That guy's car eats pizza!"  That made me chuckle for quite some time.  ||||reg||10
